  "description": "Line accounts (ARCHITECTURE decision 179, schema 70) on the track of flex-dispatch.json (nodes a to g, Alpha, Beta and Gamma with platforms; Delta and Far have none), flexible dispatch off. Main (Alpha, Gamma) and Short (Alpha, Beta, Gamma) run all day with one train in service at every level, but no train is bought, so nothing is carried or run: what the lines record is the share of the fixed costs. setEconomyMode management and setLineAccounts true, then 1501 minutes, a day and the hour that ends at 1500. Main's route is 3584 units (lineJourney: Alpha to Gamma), Short's 3584 (1536 + 2048), 64000 units a kilometre. Each hour the company pays operating 18 x 5 stations = 90 (Main 36, Short 54, as each line's stations are counted: a station two lines call at counts for both) and maintenance round(12 x 7168 / 64000 + 8 x 2) = round(17.344) = 17, shared by 8.672 : 8.672: Main 9 and Short 8 (the tie goes to the lower line, largest remainder). Day 0 has 24 hours: operating 864 and 1296, maintenance 216 and 192; day 1 has the one hour: 36 and 54, 9 and 8. Day 0's end: energy round(220 x 7168 / 64000) = round(24.64) = 25 for the routes, 12 and 13 after the tie again (Main 13), and 360 for each train, so 373 and 372; staff 620 x stations + 480 x trains, Main 620 x 2 + 480 = 1720, Short 620 x 3 + 480 = 2340. They add to the company's days (216000, 40800, 74500 and 406000 cents; day 1 9000 and 1700). Removing Short drops its records and leaves the final state with Main's alone. The fares, boardings and loads share the same books and are checked by LineAccountsTests (the lines add up to the company's day on a transfer network).",
